  "body": "Was stacked on #579 (#570, probe search limit and feed-only approach), which merged on 2026-11-10; this PR now holds only #574's change against main.\n\n## What changed\nEvery mill post now writes an explicit spindle stop between a probe's tool change and length offset and its first move. Today the probe is safe on a Tormach only because PathPilot's `M6` stops the spindle, which is a property of the control, not something the program says.\n- **Rule:** in `startPreamble`, `probeStop = spindleWait && !(sRpm > 0)`. Only a probe states 0 rpm, because tools refuse 0. After the spindle block and before coolant, the post writes the stop.\n- **Per post:**\n  - Fanuc, Haas, Tormach, Sinumerik, Heidenhain: `M5`.\n  - Mazak: `MOTOFF`, its own stop word.\n  - Fanuc Lathe: untouched (no probing).\n- **Unchanged:** cutting sections and older streams post byte-identical output.\n- **Decision record:** `docs/decisions/574-probe-m5.md`.\n\n**Stack merge (`fd1076af`):** #579 branched from a main older than #174's protected probe moves, so merging it hit conflicts in three Fanuc goldens and broke `probe_guard`. The merge commit resolves both.\n- #579's new feed from the safe plane down to the approach plane now posts as a protected move: `G31` plus the `#5063` alarm on Fanuc, `G38.3` plus the `#5070` check on Tormach.\n- `probe_guard` expects one more protected move per mode.\n- `fanuc/probe_corner.nc` and `tormach/probe_guard_moves.nc` are regenerated to match.\n\n#579 will need the same resolution when it takes main.\n\n**Golden diffs from #574 itself:** each file gains one `M5` line right after the `G43` line:\n- `fanuc/probe_bore_centre.nc`\n- `fanuc/probe_corner.nc`\n- `fanuc/probe_corner_negative.nc`\n- `fanuc/probe_edge_negative_x.nc`\n- `tormach/probe_guard_moves.nc`\n\nUntil #526 merges, some posts still write a probe's spindle start (`S0 M3`) before the new stop. The flag is computed separately, so it works in either merge order; Heidenhain will have a small hand-merge next to #526's lines.\n\n## How tested\n- **New `probe_spindle_stop`, all six mill posts:**\n  - `a_probe_section_stops_its_spindle_after_the_tool_change_on_every_mill_post`: the stop comes after the tool change and offset, before the first move, and nothing restarts the spindle. It failed before the change.\n  - `a_cutting_section_states_no_spindle_stop_before_its_first_move`: the control case.\n- **Also passing:** probe_op, probe_guard, inverted_probe, conformance, posting, tormach_post, fanuc_post, heidenhain_block_form, sinumerik_safe_retract, plus #579's probe_search, probe_pick and probe_reach, and all camcraft-post tests. Clippy (post and app) is clean.\n\n## Not exercised (draft)\nA Hub or machine run of a probe program with the new `M5`. It is a defensive stop on an already-stopped spindle.\n\nChangelog: Every mill post writes an explicit spindle stop (M5; MOTOFF on Mazak) after a probe's tool change and length offset, before its first move (#574)\n\nFixes #574\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n\n",
